-- work/tickets.cub — the tickets of the work on this repository (opened 2026-11-12). Loaded after
-- work/goals.cub. Each record says a ticket's kind, the goals it serves and whether it is open; its
-- text is the comment beginning `tN (date):` at the place it concerns (python3 tools/work.py show
-- tN prints it with its location). Tickets with no single place in the code have their text here.
-- To close a ticket: fix what it says, delete its comment at the site, and set its status to
-- `(closed #YYYYMMDD)` here in the same commit. An open ticket's status is `opened`.
--
-- t33 (2026-11-12): question. Not yet done: reading the evaluator's rule bodies (src/net.c's
-- interaction cases, src/dnf.c's face algebra) side by side with the published rules, CCHM (Cohen,
-- Coquand, Huber, Mörtberg, TYPES 2015, LIPIcs 69) and the clocked extension (Kristensen,
-- Møgelberg, Vezzosi, arXiv:2102.01969), each rule recorded as matching or deviating at its site.
-- The two papers are not in the repository; fetch them. Until this is done, conformance of the
-- implementation to the calculus is not known.
--
-- t34 (2026-11-12): question. Not yet done: reading src/lang.c's translation of terms into the
-- evaluator's graph for anything that can change a term's meaning (the strictness analysis that
-- decides which operands are built eagerly, fully lazy lifting, sweeping of compiled code, the
-- module cache, whose key is the build date and the files' texts and whose hits are trusted).
--
-- t35 (2026-11-12): question. Not yet done: reading lib/check.cub's typing clauses against the
-- calculus's typing rules, each recorded as matching or deviating at its site.
--
-- t36 (2026-11-12): needs-work. tracks/STATE.md, tracks/E-lemmas.md and tracks/TREE.md (generated)
-- were written for a reading process now recorded as tickets at the sites; their findings are
-- tickets (t7, t29), and their status claims date from before 2026-11-12. LANGUAGE.md describes the
-- x86 translator as the compiler and points at an archived plan for the trusted list. Fold what is
-- still true into README.md and the sites, and remove the rest.
--
-- t37 (2026-11-12): needs-work. tools/work.py reads tickets from the code's text (records here,
-- comments at the sites). Queries written in the language over the checked records (tickets by goal,
-- the goals a goal transitively serves, what is open under a goal) are to follow, with the command
-- evaluating them through the machine.
